  "id": "Compound::DB00503 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Ritonavir exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c8 and Cyp2b6, which are both members of the cytochrome P450 family and are involved in the metabolism of various substrates. The observed relationship between Ritonavir and Cyp2c9 is supported by the fact that Cyp2c8 and Cyp2b6 participate in similar metabolic pathways, including the oxidation of arachidonic acid, which is a key step in the metabolism of many drugs. Cyp2c9, as a member of this family, is likely to be involved in the oxidation of similar substrates, making it a plausible target for Ritonavir. The evidence suggests that Ritonavir may inhibit Cyp2c9 through a mechanism involving its binding to the enzyme, thereby affecting its ability to metabolize substrates. This relationship is further supported by the shared participation of Cyp2c8 and Cyp2b6 in metabolic pathways that are also engaged by Cyp2c9, indicating a potential functional overlap among these enzymes.",
